Drop BlobCore::clone(), which does not exist.

blob.h's Blob<> template wraps a call to a base-class clone() that cctools-port's BlobCore does
not declare. The name is qualified and BlobCore is not a dependent type, so the lookup happens
when the template is defined rather than when it is instantiated, and every C++ translation unit
that reaches this header fails. dyldinfo reaches it transitively and calls nothing in it.

--- a/cctools/ld64/src/ld/code-sign-blobs/blob.h
+++ b/cctools/ld64/src/ld/code-sign-blobs/blob.h
@@ -181,9 +181,6 @@
 		return NULL;
 	}
 	
-	BlobType *clone() const
-	{ assert(validateBlob()); return specific(this->BlobCore::clone());	}
-
 	static BlobType *readBlob(int fd)
 	{ return specific(BlobCore::readBlob(fd, _magic, sizeof(BlobType), 0), true); }
 
